WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.538
This report combines contact normalization and CASE
classification in one output For

00:00:05.562 --> 00:00:10.300
contact information blank and whitespace-only text
are normalized before COALESCE selects the

00:00:10.312 --> 00:00:15.412
first usable contact method For billing the query
makes a different decision

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.000
A missing bill is not converted to zero Instead CASE
labels it

00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:25.538
Needs review An exact zero gets No Charge then
higher tiers are

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.625
checked from specific thresholds down to the
low-value default Sometimes a fallback

00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:35.738
is appropriate for display Other times a missing
value carries data-quality meaning

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:39.838
that should remain visible Run the query and compare
the NULL bill

00:00:39.862 --> 00:00:41.512
record with the zero bill record
